  "body": "Some important stuff:\r\n\r\n>We have self hosted riot-web, matrix-synapse with own identify server (ldap based auth).\r\n>VM on VMware Debian 9, installation from package.\r\n> dpkg -l | grep synapse\r\n> ii  matrix-synapse                0.26.0-1                       all          Open federated Instant Messaging and VoIP server\r\n> ii  python-matrix-synapse-ldap3   0.1.2-1                        all          An LDAP3 auth provider for Synapse\r\n\r\n\r\nQuestion1:\r\n>Can we block in possibility of room creation if we want only few static room to be available? Or if we server admin?\r\n\r\nQuestion2:\r\n>When auth is on ldap server, if I change value in db (table users, column admin) to 1, user will become server admin?\r\n\r\nQuestion3:\r\n>When all users leave room, room exists but we cant join there anymore and we receiving \"internal server error\" (\"Failed to send to any server.\" in log of 'federation_client.py').",
